What is playwright?
    - it is an open-source framework by microsoft for automating browsers
    - It's used for end-to-end testing, web scraping and automating modern sites using
      python.

Why?
    - Cross-browser automation
    - Reliable and fast, with smart waiting and advanced selector support
    - Designed for dynamic, javascript-heavy sites

Basic program:

from playwright.sync_api import sync_playwright

with sync-playwright() as p:
    browser = p.chromium.launch(headless=True)
    page = browser.new_page()
    page.goto('https://www.google.com')
    print(page.title())
    browser.close()

Note:
    - headless = True (default) - runs browser without UI
    - headless = False runs browser with UI
    - goto() - Navigates to a webpage
    - page.title() - Retrieves the page title

interacting with web elements:
    - Locators and Actions
        - Selectors: identify elements by CSS selectors, text, role, etc.
        - Example:
            - page.fill('input[name="username"]', "myuser")
            - page.click('button[type="submit"]')
        - wait_for_selector() - Waits until element appears(import for dynamic sites)


from playwright.sync_api import sync_playwright

with sync.playwright() as p:
    browser = p.chromium.launch(headless=True)
